  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 330 PM CDT Tue Aug 11 2026\n\nAn intense subtropical ridge will strengthen and generally become\ncentered over the forecast area as we go through the remainder of\nthe week and weekend and into early next week. While temperatures\nwill increase in the next few days, the more prominent heat will\ndevelop this weekend when the low level flow is expected to\nobtain a more westerly component. An anomalous thermal ridge \nwill extend from the Southern Plains eastward into our region with\nH850 temperatures potentially approaching 27 deg C, especially in\nthe Delta region where westerly flow will be most pronounced. \nThese values if realized correlate with record high temperatures, \nbut on the flip side, the airmass would be highly mixed meaning \nthat lower RH values would help to lessen heat indices. The net \nresult should still be at least elevated levels of dangerous heat \ncontinuing through the forecast. There is currently a heat \nadvisory for Wednesday, and expect additional heat advisories as \nwe go farther out in time.\n\nIt appears the heat will peak in the Sun-Tue time frame with \ncompressional heating ahead of an approaching cold, then expect \nthe potential the ridge to break down as we go later into next \nweek. Until that happens, the increased anticyclonic flow will \nlimit diurnal convective coverage resulting in meager rainfall\ntotals. /EC/",
